3S + 1M: Building a Local AI-Powered Coding Environment

Three Software Tools, One AI Coding Model — A Complete Local AI Development Setup

1. Project Overview

The purpose of this project is to build a fully functional, locally hosted AI-assisted programming environment by integrating three essential software tools with one powerful AI coding model.

The project is based on a simple but effective concept called 3S + 1M.

* 3S (Three Softwares): Three software applications working together to create an integrated AI programming environment.
* 1M (One Model): One AI-powered coding model responsible for understanding programming instructions, generating code, analyzing existing projects, identifying bugs, and assisting with software development.

The three software tools selected for this project are:

* Ollama – A local AI model management and inference platform.
* Cline – An AI-powered coding agent that can interact with development projects, modify files, execute commands, and assist with complex programming tasks.
* Visual Studio Code (VS Code) – A powerful and extensible source-code editor that serves as the primary development interface.

The AI coding model selected for this project is:

- Qwen3-Coder – An AI coding model designed to understand programming languages, generate code, analyze software projects, solve programming problems, and assist developers with various software engineering tasks.

